{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.DualNumber","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Artinian.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Jacobson.Ideal","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TemperleyLiebTower"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.traceRadical_epsCoeff_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.traceRadical_epsCoeff_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.lean#L125-L141","doc":"**The radical of this trace is trivial**, so the counterexample is not an\nartefact of a degenerate pairing that a quotient would repair.\n\n`ℚ[ε]` *is* its own quotient by the trace radical, and it is still not\nsemisimple. So passing to `A / rad τ` — bricks 1–3 — cannot by itself rescue the\nimplication either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.nondegenerate_cyclic_trace_not_sufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.nondegenerate_cyclic_trace_not_sufficient","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.lean#L108-L123","doc":"**The headline: a non-degenerate cyclic trace does not imply semisimplicity.**\n\nPackaged as the exact conjunction that refutes any attempt to discharge\n`WenzlTowerStep`'s conclusion from its own nondegeneracy hypothesis. The witness\nis `ℚ[ε]/(ε²)`.\n\nThis is why brick 1's `quot_pairing_nondegenerate` — which makes that hypothesis\n*free* on the quotient — does not make the class easy: a free hypothesis that\ncannot carry the conclusion buys nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.dualNumber_not_isSemisimpleRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.dualNumber_not_isSemisimpleRing","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.lean#L97-L106","doc":"**But the dual numbers are not semisimple.** `ε` is a nonzero nilpotent, so\nthe ring is not reduced, and a semisimple ring is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.lean#L82-L95","doc":"**The functional is non-degenerate**, in exactly the shape\n`WenzlTowerStep.semisimple_ascend` asks for.\n\nGiven `x ≠ 0` write `x = a + bε`. If `a ≠ 0`, pairing with `ε` returns `a`; if\n`a = 0` then `b ≠ 0`, and pairing with `1` returns `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.lean#L77-L80","doc":"**The functional is cyclic** — trivially, the dual numbers commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff_apply","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.lean#L74-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.epsCoeff","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TraceNondegeneracyInsufficient.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The ε-coefficient of a dual number, as a linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0}]}